{
  "_note": "Snapshot offers read with WebFetch from public product pages on 2026-10-13 by the Ponder sourcing passes (supplier hosts are blocked to curl). Prices are per piece: pack prices were divided by the pack size, and Jameco's order multiples are set as packSize. Numeric stock is pieces on hand; counts the pages gave in packs (Adafruit 298 and 4255, Mouser 485-755, 485-298, 485-299, 485-2780, 485-4294, Printed Solid 8307) were multiplied by the pack size. stock 0 means out of stock or backorder only (those offers are kept for the record and dropped by `distinta source`). DigiKey pages did not render price or stock, and the two rows once read from regional mirrors could not be traced to a digikey.com page, so they were removed. Shipping: only SparkFun and LightingSupply.com publish a rate; every other figure is an estimate, explained in shippingBasis (shippingRead lists the one shop whose charge here is its published rate; SparkFun's free shipping over $100 is read, but its figure here is the same stand-in as the other small shops). Tariffs and duties are not included anywhere. Rows with a 'note' were re-read or corrected on 2026-10-13 after review.",
  "shippingRead": ["LightingSupply.com"],
  "shippingBasis": {
    "SparkFun": "Read: sparkfun.com/shipping, free UPS Ground when the subtotal is $100 or more (under 10 lb, contiguous US, logged in). Below $100 the rate shows only at checkout, so this is the same USPS Ground Advantage retail 1 lb Zone 8 stand-in as the other small shops (Notice 123); it is $0 for a $100+ SparkFun order.",
    "Adafruit": "ESTIMATE, probably low or high by $10-20. adafruit.com/shipping (re-read 2026-10-13): USPS Ground Advantage and Priority Mail 'only permitted for orders under $200', UPS Ground Saver 'under $500'; this order is about $900, so it ships UPS Ground, 'rounded up to the next whole pound', with dimensional weight. No UPS price is published. Stand-in: USPS Ground Advantage retail, 9 lb, Zone 8, $37.10 (Notice 123, effective 2026-10-04). 9 lb guesses the boxed weight: 41 ribbon cables at 22 g each (read on the 3890 page) are 0.9 kg; 20 Raspberry Pi 15 W supplies have no published weight (taken as about 100 g each); the small parts and box add about 1 kg. Get a cart estimate before ordering.",
    "PiShop.us": "ESTIMATE. Weight-based, rounded up to the next pound, shown at checkout; no flat rate published. Passes gave $6 and $10; the higher is kept.",
    "Mouser": "ESTIMATE. Shipping help pages showed a maintenance notice; terms say transport is paid by the customer (FCA). Insurance $0.90 at $200+ plus $0.90 per extra $100 is not included.",
    "Seeed Studio": "ESTIMATE. Ships from the China warehouse (DHL 2-5 working days); cost depends on weight and shows only at checkout. DAP terms: US duties are extra and NOT included (Seeed's customs page cites a 45% base tariff on dev boards).",
    "Jameco": "ESTIMATE. Rates computed at checkout (UPS/FedEx/USPS by weight). Read: $10 minimum order, $5 processing fee under $10.",
    "LightingSupply.com": "Read: https://lightingsupply.com/pages/ordering-shipping, $14.99 on orders $0.01 to $100.00, contiguous US.",
    "Grand Brass": "ESTIMATE. Shipping page could not be read. USPS Ground Advantage retail, 18 lb, Zone 8, $68.60 (Notice 123, effective 2026-10-04). 18 lb: 20 goosenecks at the design's 320 g estimate (6.4 kg; no weight published) plus 40 couplings, 40 nuts and 40 nipples (about 1.2 kg from their steel volume) and packing. Weigh one gooseneck and get a checkout quote.",
    "Dale Electric Supply": "ESTIMATE. No small-order rate published. USPS Ground Advantage retail, 1 lb, Zone 8 (Notice 123), as an upper bound.",
    "Wagner Companies": "ESTIMATE. Buyer pays freight; no rate published. 40 disks x 0.469 lb = 18.8 lb: USPS Ground Advantage retail, 20 lb, Zone 8 (Notice 123), as an upper bound.",
    "Pololu": "ESTIMATE. No dollar rates on pololu.com/ordering. USPS Ground Advantage retail, 1 lb, Zone 8 (Notice 123), as an upper bound.",
    "Bolt Depot": "ESTIMATE. No small-order rate on boltdepot.com/Service. USPS Ground Advantage retail, 1 lb, Zone 8 (Notice 123), as an upper bound.",
    "Printed Solid": "ESTIMATE. Free above $50 (contiguous US); this order is below that and no paid rate is shown. USPS Ground Advantage retail, 1 lb, Zone 8 (Notice 123), as an upper bound.",
    "Master Electronics": "ESTIMATE. The shipping pages of masterelectronics.com and onlinecomponents.com could not be fetched. USPS Ground Advantage retail, 2 lb, Zone 8, $19.80 (read from https://pe.usps.com/text/dmm300/Notice123.htm, effective 2026-10-04); 20 speakers at 25 g are about 1.1 lb before packing."
  },
